From: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] uci: serialize conditional package updates and preserve publication state

A conditional configuration owner must load, check and publish against the
same inode lifetime as ordinary save, commit and revert users. Retain package
locks across atomic replacement, provide nonblocking acquisition before load,
and preserve saved edits until configuration publication succeeds.

Check output, synchronization and rename failures without consuming unpublished
changes. Report already-published state distinctly so a caller does not blindly
replay non-idempotent deltas. The public context and error interface require
a matching libuci consumer ABI; session and wireless policy remain outside UCI.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>
---

